# Build context: ALLOWLIST, not blocklist.
#
# Everything is excluded, then the seven inputs the image is built from are
# re-admitted. A blocklist has to be updated every time the repository gains a
# directory, and the failure mode of forgetting is silent: the new directory is
# uploaded to the build daemon and cached there. With an allowlist the failure
# mode is a build error naming the missing path, which is the direction a
# security-relevant default should fail.
#
# What "excluded" buys: nothing that is not listed below is ever sent to the
# builder, so it cannot land in a layer, in the build cache, or on a remote
# builder host. That covers the local .env, editor scratch directories, an
# unrelated git worktree sitting under the repo, node_modules, test fixtures and
# every credential-shaped file this tree can accumulate.
#
# `dist/` is excluded too, deliberately: the image compiles from src/ in its own
# build stage, so a stale or hand-edited dist/ on the builder's disk can never
# become the code that runs in the container.
#
# Do NOT remove tastytrade-llms-txt-docs. Several static MCP resources read
# markdown out of that directory with readFileSync at module load, so the
# server crashes on startup without it. See the Dockerfile.

# 1. Deny everything.
*

# 2. Re-admit exactly the build inputs.
#
#    package.json + package-lock.json  reproducible install (and the runtime
#                                      version read by src/version.ts)
#    tsconfig.json + src               the TypeScript build
#    tastytrade-llms-txt-docs          RUNTIME dependency (see above)
#    LICENSE                           shipped in the runtime image. MIT requires
#                                      the notice to be included in all copies,
#                                      and a published image is one.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src
!tastytrade-llms-txt-docs
!LICENSE

# 3. Re-deny anything env-shaped or VCS-shaped that could be nested inside an
#    admitted tree. Secrets are supplied at run time with --env-file or -e,
#    never copied into a layer, and never uploaded to a builder. The `**/`
#    prefix matters: a bare `.env*` is anchored at the context root and would
#    not match a nested one.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
